NNAAMMEE
     aarrcchh, mmaacchhiinnee — print architecture type

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aarrcchh [--kkss]
     mmaacchhiinnee [--aa]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aarrcchh and mmaacchhiinnee commands display the machine's architecture in
     slightly different ways.  aarrcchh by default displays the application archi‐
     tecture, defined by both the operating system and the instruction set ar‐
     chitecture, while mmaacchhiinnee displays the kernel architecture (without the
     operating system part).  Note that both commands output the target archi‐
     tecture as opposed to uname(1) which describes the host.  This is useful
     for dynamic discovery of the target architecture in build or configura‐
     tion scripts needing to work in cross-compilation environments.

     The options for aarrcchh are as follows:

     --kk      Display the kernel architecture instead of application architec‐
             ture.

     --ss      Display the chosen architecture in a short form, i.e., without
             the operating system prefixed.

     The options for mmaacchhiinnee are as follows:

     --aa      Display the application architecture instead of the kernel archi‐
             tecture.

